<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Guiscard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1015–<a href="/years/1085">1085</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Guiscard was a Norman adventurer of the Hauteville family who became Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> in 1059. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> in 1071, ending Byzantine rule in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and conquered Amalfi in 1073 and Salerno in 1076. With his brother Roger he began the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, and he later campaigned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-guiscard.jpg" alt="Robert Guiscard" width="250" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_Guiscard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
